e Inverse Walsh-Hadamard Transform yields the values for $X_j$:\n$X_0 = -3/31$\n$X_1 = 29/31$\n$X_2 = 21/31$\n$X_3 = 3/31$\n$X_4 = 5/31$\n$X_5 = 0$\n$X_6 = 5/31$\n$X_7 = 12/31$\n\nUsing the relation $2x_j - 1 = (-1)^j X_j$, we solve for the relative cut positions $x_j$:\n- $j=0: 2x_0 - 1 = -3/31 \\implies x_0 = 14/31$\n- $j=1: 2x_1 - 1 = -29/31 \\implies x_1 = 1/31$\n- $j=2: 2x_2 - 1 = 21/31 \\implies x_2 = 26/31$\n- $j=3: 2x_3 - 1 = -3/31 \\implies x_3 = 14/31$\n- $j=4: 2x_4 - 1 = 5/31 \\implies x_4 = 18/31$\n- $j=5: 2x_5 - 1 = 0 \\implies x_5 = 1/2$\n- $j=6: 2x_6 - 1 = 5/31 \\implies x_6 = 18/31$\n- $j=7: 2x_7 - 1 = -12/31 \\implies x_7 = 19/62$\n\nFinally, adding the relative positions to the start of each valid slot $t_j = 3j + 1 + x_j$ gives the exact rational coordinates of each consensus-halving cut.\n\n<answer>45/31, 125/31, 243/31, 324/31, 421/31, 33/2, 607/31, 1383/62</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 69.5, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "medium", "escalation_round": 1}
