../2302.04718/README.md:21:The certificate is produced mechanically by exact modular Gaussian elimination in (O(n^3)). At shipping (n=104), the measured generic implementation averaged **67,337 field operations, 95 inversions, and 0.001855 seconds**. This is fast software and therefore rules out Track A, but is far beyond unaided hand execution. The compact route recognizes the row/column permutation of (J-I): compute (S=(n-1)^{-1}sum_j b_j), then (x_i=S-b_j) at the unique point missed by (H_i). It takes exactly **208 field operations**; recognizing and accurately executing those 31-bit modular operations is the Track B test.
